('alict_01628', 12, 'General ICT', 'A security system uses an 8-bit access code to determine entry permissions. The system applies a bitwise AND operation to verify if a user''s access code allows entry to a restricted area. wdrlaIl wjir 8-bit bv fokafkao hkak bitwise AND fufyhqula fhdohs'' If the stored access code is 10101100 and the user''s code is 10000100, what will be the result of the bitwise AND operation between these two codes?', '["10101100", "10000100", "00101000", "00000100", "00000000"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The question asks to do AND operation for 10101100 and 10000100. m%Yakh 101011002 100001002 Here we use the AND gate to produce the answer. wms ICN A B F 1 0 2 0 1 0 3 1 0 4 1 As the above truth we can do the calculation given in the question', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1628, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01629', 12, 'General ICT', 'What is the first computer that could store programs?', '["EDVAC", "ENIAC", "UNIVAC", "EDSAC", "IBM 704"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: This was designed based on the stored-program proposed by John von Neumann in 1945. Unlike its predecessor which required manual EDV AC could store and modify its instructions in memory', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1629, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
