('alict_01693', 12, 'General ICT', 'what is the most simplified expression of A̅B + AB + A̅B̅ + B̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅ of the followings?', '["AB\u0305", "0", "1", "A\u0305B\u0305", "A+B"]'::jsonb, 1, 'A Boolean expression is obtained and then simplified using Boolean laws. Q = A̅B + AB + A̅B̅ + B̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅ = (A.̅ B̅̅̅̅̅). ( A. B̅̅̅̅̅). (A.̅ B̅̅̅̅̅̅) . B ̅ De morgan''s Law = ( A̿ + B̅). (A̅ + B̅). (A̿ + B̿). B̅ De morgan''s Law = (A + B̅). (A̅ + B̅)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1693, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01694', 12, 'General ICT', 'Among the number of bits possible for and Mantissa in IEEE 754 - Double Precision IEEE 754 - Double Precision Exponent Mantissa ioyd yels 4) Explanation', '["1, 11, 32", "1, 7, 24", "1, 8, 23", "1, 11, 52", "1, 12, 33 The"]'::jsonb, 4, 'We compare each pair of bits to determine the correct output for the Bitwise XOR between the binary numbers 110100012 and 011011112. The XOR operation results in 1 if the bits are different and 0 if they are the same', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1694, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01695', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following circuits does the same logic tl iudk ;¾lhla 1) Let''s get the answer below', '["101111102", "000011102", "101001012", "111111112", "010000012 A B C"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "111111112".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1695, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01696', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following conversions are correct?', '["A only. A", "C only. C", "A and B only. A B", "B and C only. B C", "A and C only. A C"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Let''s now convert each number into its binary form to verify whether the given conversions are accurate', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1696, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01697', 12, 'General ICT', 'The total number of students in a primary school is 1010001002. Half of them are boys. The number of girls isiqka .Kk 1010001002 bka wvla <uqka 3) Explanation', '["101000002", "160", "2428", "B216", "101000112 6"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "101000002".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1697, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01698', 12, 'General ICT', 'What is the output of F in the following logic F 4) Explanation', '["A", "A\u0305", "0", "1", "Can''t say for"]'::jsonb, 3, 'This Boolean expression can be simplified as follows. N̅ + AS̅A̅̅̅̅̅ + A N̅ + A̅ + S̿ + A̅ + A De Morgan''s Law N̅ + A̅ + S + A̅ + A Double inverse law N̅ + S + A̅ + 1 Inverse law 1 Identity law', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1698, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01699', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following is an example of a multi-tasking operating nyq ld¾h 1) Explanation', '["Windows 10", "MS-DOS", "IMB Mainframe", "Linux Server", "None of the lsisjla Option"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Windows 10".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1699, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01700', 12, 'General ICT', 'In 1890 ................................................ used punch card concepts to invent ..................................... Most suitable words that can be used to fill in the blanks 1890', '["Joseph Electrical weaving loom", "Charles Babbage , Analytical Engine", "Howard Mark 1", "Blesie Adding Machine", "Herman Electric Mechanical Calculator"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Option 1: Joseph Jacquard used punch card technology to control a mechanical which was a precursor to computing devices. this was not in 1890 and the term "Electrical Weaving Loom" is not accurate. Jacquard''s loom was a mechanical not an electrical one. Joseph Jacquard', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1700, 'A/L Past Paper Series')
