('alict_01702', 12, 'General ICT', 'What will be the output of this code?', '["3", "5", "10", "Infinite loop", "Error"]'::jsonb, 1, '• count = 0 Initializes the variable to 0. This will be used to control the while loop. • while count Enters the loop as long as is less than 5. Will repeat until the condition becomes false or a break occurs', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1702, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01703', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which historical computing system is considered the first electronic general-purpose digital computer?', '["ENIAC", "UNIV AC I", "MARK 1", "UNIV AC", "IBM 701"]'::jsonb, 1, 'This question is asking which early computer was the first ever to be fully and capable of solving general-purpose problems (not just one specific task). That means it could be reprogrammed and used for many kinds of calculations', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1703, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01704', 12, 'General ICT', 'what is the most simplified expression of (A + B̅̅̅̅̅̅̅) + (A + B̅ + C̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅) + A̅B + (ABC̅̅̅̅̅̅̅) + C of the followings?', '["A + B + C", "A + B", "A + B\u0305 + C", "A. B. C", "A\u0305 + B\u0305 + C"]'::jsonb, 5, 'A Boolean expression is obtained and then simplified using Boolean laws F = (A + B̅̅̅̅̅̅̅) + (A + B̅ + C̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅) + A̅B + (ABC̅̅̅̅̅̅̅) + C = A̅. B̅ + (A + B̅ + C̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅) + A̅B + (ABC̅̅̅̅̅̅̅) + C De morgan''s Law = A̅. B̅ + A̅. B̿. C̅ + A̅B + A. B', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1704, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01705', 12, 'General ICT', 'What will be the output of this code?', '["A", "B", "C", "A C", "Error Answer"]'::jsonb, 1, '• x = 10 This line assigns the value 10 to the variable x. Wherever x it means the number 10. • if x we check if the value of x (which is 10) is greater than 5. Since 10 enters this if block and checks the next condition nested inside it. fuys" wms x w', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1705, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01706', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following logic expressions simplifies to A ⊕ B?', '["A. B\u0305 + A\u0305. B", "(A + B). (A. B)", "(A\u0305. B\u0305) + (A. B)", "(A + B\u0305). (A\u0305 + B)", "(A. B) + (A\u0305. B\u0305)"]'::jsonb, 1, 'XOR (exclusive OR) outputs 1 only when exactly one input is 1 and the other is 0. XOR (exclusive OR) 1 - A = 0, B = 0 → Output = 0 - A = 0, B = 1 → Output = 1 - A = 1, B = 0 → Output = 1 - A = 1, B = 1 → Output = 0 So XOR is true only when inputs are different', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1706, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01707', 12, 'General ICT', 'What is the output of the below o@ x = 7 y = 2 z = (x ** y)', '["12", "12.25", "17.00", "17", "25.5 Let''s follow the calculation step by step"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "17".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1707, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01708', 12, 'General ICT', 'What will be the if 1, 0, and 3 are given as the input?', '["The result of 1 is 1 The result of 0 is 1 The result of 3 is 6", "The result of 1 is 1 The result of 0 is 0 The result of 3 is 6", "The result of 1 is 1 The result of 0 is 1 The result of 3 is 3", "The result of 1 is 1 The result of 0 is 0 The result of 3 is 3", "The result of 1 is 1 The result of 0 is 1 The result of 3 is 9 The result of 1 is 1 The result of 0 is 1 The result of 3 is 6 9"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "The result of 1 is 1 The result of 0 is 1 The result of 3 is 6".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1708, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
