('alict_01731', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the Which of the following statements correctly distinguishes Second Generation computers (1956-1963) from Third Generation computers (1964-1971)?', '["Second Generation used integrated while Third Generation used transistors. fojk", "Second Generation computers were and more reliable than Third Generation computers. fojk", "Second Generation computers primarily used assembly language and machine whereas Third Generation computers introduced high-level languages like COBOL and FORTRAN more extensively. fojk", "Second Generation computers supported but Third Generation computers did not. fojk", "Both Second and Third Generation computers used vacuum but with different configurations. fojk"]'::jsonb, 3, '• Option 1 - Transistors were used in Second while Integrated Circuits (ICs) were introduced in Third Generation. • Option 2 - The opposite is true. Third Generation machines were more and consumed less power', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1731, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01732', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following statements best describes the difference between low -level and high -level programming languages?', '["Low-level languages are while high-level languages are platform-dependent", "Low-level languages are closer to machine while high-level languages are closer to human language", "Low-level languages provide automatic memory while high-level languages require manual memory handling", "Low-level languages are always easier to while high-level languages are always harder to maintain", "Low-level languages are designed only for web while high-level languages are designed for embedded systems"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Incorrect. Low-level languages (like Assembly) are highly dependent on the hardware while many high-level languages (like Python or Java) are designed to be platform-independent. Option 2: Correct', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1732, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01733', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following statements is NOT true about the difference between an interpreter and a compiler?', '["An interpreter executes the program line by while a compiler translates the entire program into machine code before execution", "Interpreted languages are generally slower than compiled languages", "An interpreter provides immediate feedback on while a compiler might wait until the entire program is translated", "Compilers are typically used for system while interpreters are often used for scripting languages", "Both interpreters and compilers require the same hardware to function"]'::jsonb, 5, 'The Python code starts with x = 15 and y = 10 and then checks whether x is greater than which is true in this case. It then proceeds to the next checking if x % y == 0, which evaluates to false because 15 % 10 results in a remainder of 5', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1733, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
