('alict_01773', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following is an example of a partial dependency?', '["A teacher''s ID determines the teacher''s and the name determines the teacher''s office number", "A student''s ID determines their enrollment and the enrollment status determines the department they are enrolled in", "A course code determines the course which determines the course duration", "A customer''s order ID determines the product but the product details depend on the product ID", "A car''s VIN number determines its and year of manufacture"]'::jsonb, 4, 'A partial dependency occurs in a database when a non-prime attribute is dependent on a part of a composite primary rather than the entire key. It typically arises in a relation where a composite key and one of its components can determine certain non-prime attributes', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1773, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
