('alict_01839', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following is an example of a digital computer?', '["Analog Computer", "Speedometer", "Hybrid Computer", "ENIAC", "Punch card machine"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Analog Computer Analog computers process information represented by continuous physical quantities. They are used for simulating real-world such as temperature and by using voltages or mechanical parts. They do not work with discrete values like digital computers. fhdod', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1839, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
