('alict_01844', 12, 'General ICT', 'Among the number of bits possible for and Mantissa in IEEE 754 - Double Precision', '["1, 11, 32 In this the sign bit is correctly assigned 1 bit. the exponent and mantissa bits do not add up correctly to 64 bits. The exponent is given 11 bits (which is correct), but the mantissa is given only 32 resulting in a total of 44 bits when combined with the sign which is incorrect", "1, 7, 24 In this the sign bit is correctly assigned 1 bit. the exponent is given 7 and the mantissa 24 totaling only 32 which is the format for single not double precision", "10001101", "11100011", "11101111"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "11100011".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1844, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01845', 12, 'General ICT', 'What will be the output of the below code?', '["[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]", "[8, 6, 4, 2, 7, 5, 3, 1]", "[2, 8, 6, 4, 5, 3, 7, 1]", "[8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1]", "[2, 4, 6, 8, 1, 3, 5, 7]"]'::jsonb, 5, '• First_numbers = [num for num in numbers if num % 2 == 0] This is a list comprehension that loops over each num in the numbers list. It filters out even numbers (numbers where the remainder when divided by 2 is 0). All the even numbers are collected in the list First_numbers', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1845, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
