('alict_01851', 12, 'General ICT', 'EWW + EWW What is the answer when this is simplified?', '["EWW + EW", "WW + EW", "WE + EW", "W", "WE"]'::jsonb, 3, '= EWW + EWW = (E + W)W + E(W + W) De Morgan''s Law = (E + W)W + E(W) Idempotent Law = EW + WW + EW Distributive Law = EW + 0 + EW Inverse Law = EW + EW Identity Law', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1851, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01852', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following is not a benefit of utilizing universal gates when implementing logic circuits?', '["Reducing the number of different types of gates needed in a circuit", "Increasing of overall size and complexity of a circuit", "Reducing the overall heat generation", "Increasing the power efficiency", "Reducing the manufacturing costs"]'::jsonb, 2, 'This is not a benefit of utilizing universal gates when implementing logic circuits', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1852, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01853', 12, 'General ICT', 'What does Single Sign-On (SSO) allow users to do?', '["Sign in to multiple accounts with different credentials", "Sign in to multiple accounts with a single set of credentials", "Sign in to a single account with different credentials", "Sign in to a single account with multiple sets of credentials", "Sign in to an account without any credentials"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Single Sign-On (SSO) is a user authentication process that allows users to log in to multiple applications or systems using just one set of login credentials (such as a username and password)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1853, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01854', 12, 'General ICT', 'Final output', '["A", "A\u0305", "1", "0", "B"]'::jsonb, 2, 'UPDATE is the SQL keyword used to modify existing records in a table. The syntax for using the UPDATE keyword is as UPDATE tablename SET column1 = value1, column2 = value2, ... WHERE The WHERE clause specifies which record or records that should be updated', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1854, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01855', 12, 'General ICT', 'Match Which development most accurately marked a critical shift from isolated computing to integrated ICT beyond just technical progress?', '["The introduction of the first personal microprocessor in the 1970s. 1970", "The rise of graphical user interfaces in consumer operating systems", "The commercialization of the World Wide Web in the early 1990s. 1990", "The invention of packet switching by Paul Baran and Donald Davies. Paul Baran Donald Davies", "The mass production of floppy disks enabling portable storage. f.k hd yels"]'::jsonb, 3, 'This question tests the ability to distinguish between technological inventions and the socio -technical tipping points that defined the ICT era''s emergence - where information and communication merged into a unified force affecting all domains. m%Yakh Option Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1855, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01856', 12, 'General ICT', 'What does the mode ''r+'' do when opening a file?', '["Opens a file for reading only", "Opens a file for writing only f.dkqjla", "Opens a file for writing creating a new file if it doesn''t exist", "Opens a file for reading creating a new file if it doesn''t exist", "Opens a file for reading and starting at the beginning of the file"]'::jsonb, 5, 'The mode r+ in file handling opens a file for both reading and starting at the beginning of the file. It does not create a new file if it doesn''t unlike some other modes. This means you can read from and write to the file without truncating its contents. f', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1856, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01857', 12, 'General ICT', 'Plagiarism can best be defined as', '["Copying someone else''s work and citing the source", "Using open-source content for commercial use", "Submitting another person''s work as your own", "Creating original content based on multiple sources. nyq", "Using software without a license"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Plagiarism refers to presenting someone else''s or words as your own without proper credit. It is a serious ethical violation in and creative fields. Option 1: Incorrect because copying and citing is not plagiarism - citation gives credit', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1857, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01858', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following developments most directly enabled the transition from additive number systems to positional marking a pivotal moment in the history of numerical abstraction?', '["The invention of Roman numerals by the ancient Romans. frdaujreka", "The introduction of tally marks in prehistoric record-keeping. m%d.a", "The creation of the base-60 system by the Babylonians", "The use of abaci in ancient Chinese commerce", "The adoption of the Hindu-Arabic numeral system in medieval Europe"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option Incorrect. Roman numerals are a classic additive system. They lacked a place value making arithmetic operations cumbersome and limiting abstraction. frdau wxl Option Incorrect. Tally marks are a primitive additive representation with no concept of base or position', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1858, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01859', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following is a part of a closed system of the human isref¾ fldgila 2) Let''s consider each option one by one', '["Ear", "Heart", "Eye", "Lung", "Kidney"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Ear".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1859, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01860', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following correctly represents a classification of systems?', '["System components and boundaries", "Closed and open systems", "System errors and failures", "System goals and objectives", "System inputs and outputs"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Closed and open systems".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1860, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01861', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following is a feature of a manual system compared to an automated system?', '["Higher speed of processing", "Greater accuracy", "Increased consistency", "Reduced labor costs", "Greater susceptibility to human error"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Option 1: This option is incorrect. Automated systems generally have a higher speed of processing compared to manual systems because they can perform tasks faster without breaks. tjka Option 2: This option is incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1861, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01862', 12, 'General ICT', 'In the magical world of a wizard stores his spells in a file called spellbook.txt. Each line in the file contains a spell name and its power level separated by a colon (:). The wizard wants to find the most powerful spell in his spellbook. Complete the following code to help him achieve this. Pythonia', '["0 \"r\" max_power power spell", "-1 \"w\" power max_power power", "None \"a\"\" spell max_power", "100 \"x\" line", "-1 \"x\" max_power power line"]'::jsonb, 1, '"max_power" is set to 0 to track the highest power level. "most_powerful_spell" is an empty string to store the name of the most powerful spell. File The file is opened in read mode ("r"). A for loop reads each line in the file. f', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1862, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01863', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which type of system is best characterized by its ability to self-regulate and maintain stability?', '["Open systems", "Closed systems", "Living systems", "Physical systems", "Manmade systems"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Open systems interact with their environment by exchanging or information. While they can adapt to external they don''t have the same intrinsic self -regulation mechanisms as living systems. They rely on external inputs to maintain their stability', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1863, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
