('alict_01865', 12, 'General ICT', 'In an office equipped with a smart management which scenario is least likely to happen?', '["Employees receive automated notifications about meeting times and changes in schedules", "The system automatically adjusts room temperatures based on occupancy and preferences of employees. fiajlhska", "The smart lighting adjusts based on time of day and employee presence to enhance energy efficiency", "Employees must manually log their attendance using a digital app that requires periodic validation of their identity. fiajlhska Tjqkaf.a", "The system provides real-time analytics on workspace helping management optimize layouts"]'::jsonb, 4, 'A smart system is a technology framework that enhances efficiency and convenience through and data analysis. iqyqre myiqj Let''s find the option that is least aligned with the principles of a smart management system', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1865, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01866', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following statements is correct with respect to openness and closeness of a system?', '["A solar power generation system is a close system", "An Automatic Teller Machine of a bank should be a close system. iajhxl%Sh", "A general-purpose computer can be considered as an open system", "A mobile phone is a close system", "Human blood circulatory system is an open system"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "A general-purpose computer can be considered as an open system".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1866, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01867', 12, 'General ICT', 'The Puzzle of the Glitching Portal Glitching oajdrfha the popular online game players are trying to activate an ancient portal that leads to a hidden level. the portal is glitching and only activates under specific conditions. According to the portal''s activation is contro lled by three mystical the Rune of Power (P), the Rune of Wisdom (W), and the Rune of Balance ud¾..; l%Svdjla l%Svlhska fmkajk oajdrhla il%sh flfia oajdrh il%sh Odjk portal activates (output Q = 1) if', '["Q = (P AND W) AND (NOT B)", "Q = (P OR W) AND (NOT B)", "Q = (P AND W) OR (NOT B)", "Q = (P OR W) OR (NOT B)", "Q = (P AND B) AND (NOT W)"]'::jsonb, 3, '• "The Rune of Power (P) is active AND the Rune of Wisdom (W) is active": This translates to P AND W. P AND W • "The Rune of Balance (B) is NOT active": This translates to NOT B. NOT B • "OR": The two conditions are combined using an OR operation. fldkafoais fol OR fufyhqula', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1867, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
