('alict_01870', 12, 'General ICT', 'The two main ways in which systems can be divided', '["Major systems and subsystems", "Natural and complex systems", "Open and closed systems", "Hybrid and structured systems", "Digital and Analog Systems"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The two main ways to categorize systems are into open systems and closed systems. This classification refers to how systems interact with their Open systems These systems interact with their environment by exchanging or energy', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1870, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01871', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following is a key characteristic of an open system?', '["Completely self-contained", "Independent of its environment", "Continuously interacts with its environment", "Only exchanges matter with the environment", "Operates in a closed loop without feedback"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: This is not a characteristic of an open system. Open systems are characterized by their interactions with the external meaning they are not self-contained. Option 2: This statement is incorrect for an open system', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1871, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
