('alict_01905', 12, 'General ICT', 'What is the default subnet mask for a Class C IPv4 address?', '["255.0.0.0", "255.255.0.0", "255.255.255.0", "255.255.255.255", "255.0.255.0"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The default subnet mask for a Class C IPv4 address is 255.255.255.0. Class C IPv4 addresses are typically used for small to medium-sized allowing for up to 254 host addresses per network (since 2 addresses are reserved for network address and broadcast address)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1905, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01906', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which deployment method involves running the new system and the old system simultaneously to ensure a smooth transition and to compare their outputs before fully switching to the new system?', '["Direct Deployment", "Parallel Deployment", "Pilot Deployment", "Phased Deployment", "Incremental Deployment"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: According to this it''s false. Direct Deployment involves switching from the old system to the new system all at without running both simultaneously. th folu Option 2: According to this it''s true', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1906, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01907', 12, 'General ICT', 'Among a half-duplex communication method', '["Walkie-talkies", "Video conferencing", "Online games", "Phone calls", "Discussions fjdals fgdals"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Walkie-talkies This is a classic example of half-duplex communication. Only one person can speak at a time while the other listens. They need to use a push-to-talk button to switch roles', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1907, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01908', 12, 'General ICT', 'In a smart home security which sensor is primarily used to detect unauthorized human movement inside a room?', '["PIR Sensor", "Temperature Sensor", "Soil Moisture Sensor", "Pressure Sensor", "Accelerometer"]'::jsonb, 1, 'PIR (Passive Infrared) Sensor Detects infrared radiation emitted by humans → perfect for motion detection. 2) Temperature Sensor Measures not suitable for intrusion detection. 3) Soil Moisture Sensor Used in not home security', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1908, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01909', 12, 'General ICT', 'What is the main difference between Pure ALOHA and Slotted ALOHA?', '["Slotted ALOHA uses time slots for transmission. Slotted ALOHA", "Pure ALOHA allows fewer collisions. Pure ALOHA u.ska", "Slotted ALOHA has no retransmission mechanism. Slotted ALOHA", "Pure ALOHA is used in wired networks only. Pure ALOHA ,nkafka", "Slotted ALOHA eliminates the need for random access. Slotted ALOHA"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: True. The key difference between Pure ALOHA and Slotted ALOHA is that Slotted ALOHA divides time into discrete time and transmissions can only start at the beginning of a time reducing the probability of collisions. mrdihka Option 2: False', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1909, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01910', 12, 'General ICT', 'An online shopping platform needs to provide a smooth user experience and load pages even during peak shopping hours. Which type of requirement does this represent?', '["Functional requirement - it describes an action the system must perform", "Non-functional requirement - it specifies performance aspects of the system", "Functional requirement - it provides core features to users", "Non-functional requirement - it details the system''s availability times", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is 2) Non-functional requirement - it specifies performance aspects of the system. This is true because the requirement describes how the system should such as loading pages quickly and providing a smooth user experience during peak hours', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1910, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01911', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following is an example of artificial ljrla o? A. Genetic algorithms', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "C only. C", "A and B only. A B", "All of the above"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Artificial Intelligence (AI) refers to computer systems that can perform tasks typically requiring human such as pattern and learning from experience. udkj Option as genetic algorithms are an example of AI', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1911, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01912', 12, 'General ICT', 'A company sells its products only through a website. it opens a shop in town to attract more customers. What type of business model does the company have now?', '["Pure Click", "Pure brick", "Brick-and-Click", "Online Only", "Shop Only"]'::jsonb, 3, 'At the company used only a website to sell this is called a Pure Click business. they opened a physical shop. Now they use both online and offline methods to sell. This type of business is called a Brick -and-Click model', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1912, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01913', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which networking device helps in reducing amplitude distortion?', '["Amplifiers", "Filters", "Repeaters", "Modems", "Antennas"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Amplifiers According to this it''s false. Amplifiers boost the signal strength but can also amplify noise and so they do not specifically reduce amplitude distortion. 2) Filters False', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1913, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01914', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following is an example of a B2C company?', '["Alibaba", "Amazon Business", "Shopify", "IBM", "UPS"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Shopify is an example of a B2C (business-to-consumer) company because it provides a platform for businesses to create and manage online allowing them to sell products directly to consumers. Shopify', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1914, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01915', 12, 'General ICT', 'What is the correct answer to the blanks in the following column?', '["Internet Banking", "Cash on Delivery", "Payment Gateway", "Credit Cards", "Check Transaction"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Payment Gateway".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1915, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01916', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following tasks uses multi software agent systems?', '["Image analysis", "Medical diagnosis", "Refinary controller", "Part picking robot", "Interactive ICT tutor"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Involves processing images using algorithms. Typically handled by a single not multiple agents. Option 2: Involves multiple specialists or tools analyzing test results). Can benefit from multiple agents collaborating to make a diagnosis', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1916, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01917', 12, 'General ICT', 'Considering the ATM as a which of the following is a functional requirement?', '["It should have an easy-to-use interface", "Security of a transaction must be ensured", "It should be possible to verify the user''s identity with the ATM card and password. ATM", "Must be able to get money in 15 seconds", "The maximum amount available should not exceed 2 lakhs"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "It should be possible to verify the user''s identity with the ATM card and password. ATM".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1917, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01918', 12, 'General ICT', 'A tutoring robot detects a student''s subtle frustration but continues giving the same tasks without adjustment. Which long-term effect is most likely?', '["Improved learning efficiency", "Student engagement trust erodes", "Emotional state has no effect", "System becomes more adaptive over time", "Student automatically adjusts to robot"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Student engagement trust erodes".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1918, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01919', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following is a valid IPv4 multicast address range?', '["224.0.0.0 to 239.255.255.255", "192.168.0.0 to 192.168.255.255", "172.16.0.0 to 172.31.255.255", "10.0.0.0 to 10.255.255.255", "169.254.0.0 to 169.254.255.255"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "224.0.0.0 to 239.255.255.255".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1919, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01920', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of these is not an e-business income stream?', '["Online trading", "Charging commissions", "Subscription", "Web Marketing", "Advertising"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "Web Marketing".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1920, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01921', 12, 'General ICT', 'In B2C who are the primary buyers ?', '["Businesses", "Consumers", "Governments rchka", "Investors wdfhdaclhska", "Retailers"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Consumers".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1921, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01922', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following best describes the digital economy?', '["An economy that relies solely on traditional manufacturing", "An economy driven by the use of digital technologies and online platforms", "An economy based exclusively on physical retail stores", "An economy that avoids using the internet for transactions. .kqfokq", "An economy focused only on government-funded projects. rcfhka"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The best description of the digital economy is 2) An economy driven by the use of digital technologies and online platforms. fufyhjkq ,nk This option highlights the role of digital technologies and online which are fundamental aspects of the digital economy', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1922, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01923', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which statement about reverse auction is correct?', '["Sellers earn more profits", "This involves one buyer and many ioyd", "Many buyers participate and the seller makes a", "The buyer must buy whatever the seller sells", "Goods are sold at the highest price"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "This involves one buyer and many ioyd".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1923, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01924', 12, 'General ICT', 'A freelance graphic designer uses an online marketplace to offer their services directly to companies. What type of business model does this belong to?', '["B2C", "B2B", "C2C", "C2B", "G2C"]'::jsonb, 4, 'This scenario describes a Consumer-to-Business (C2B) business where an individual (the consumer) provides services or products directly to businesses', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1924, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01925', 12, 'General ICT', 'What is the primary security issue associated with devices in smart homes?', '["High electricity bills", "Poor connectivity", "Vulnerability to hacking and unauthorized access", "Complexity of installation", "Lack of aesthetic design"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Vulnerability to hacking and unauthorized access".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1925, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01926', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following is true regarding the propagation of electromagnetic waves in networking?', '["Electromagnetic waves cannot travel through vacuum", "Electromagnetic waves always travel at the same speed regardless of the medium", "Electromagnetic waves with higher frequencies have shorter wavelengths", "Electromagnetic waves cannot be affected by obstacles in their path", "Electromagnetic waves can only propagate in a straight line"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The statement 3 is true according to the relationship between frequency and wavelength in electromagnetic as described by the equation λ = c frequency. λ = c / f u', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1926, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01927', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following statements belongs to pure click business style?', '["A only. A", "A and B only. A B", "B and D only. B D", "C only. C", "All of the above"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Pure click business style refers to businesses that operate entirely online without any physical storefront. These businesses provide their products or services exclusively through the internet', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1927, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01928', 12, 'General ICT', 'A company manufactures and sells skincare products directly to consumers through its own traditional retail stores. What type of business model is this?', '["Business-to-Business (B2B)", "Business-to-Consumer (B2C)", "Direct-to-Consumer (DTC)", "Consumer-to-Business (C2B)", "Franchise Model"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Direct-to-Consumer (DTC)".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1928, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01929', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following is true about a wave?', '["Amplitude affects the intensity of the wave", "Amplitude affects the frequency", "Amplitude does not affect the loudness of sound", "Amplitude does not affect the energy of the wave", "Higher amplitude means a higher pitch"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct statement is that amplitude affects the intensity of the wave. In a the amplitude is the maximum displacement of the wave from its equilibrium position. The which is a measure of the energy transmitted by the is directly proportional to the square of the amplitude', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1929, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01930', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which type of digital marketing is most effective for engaging audiences in real-time?', '["Search engine optimization (SEO)", "Email newsletters", "Live streaming events", "Whitepapers", "Print advertisements"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Live streaming allows businesses to interact with their audience instantly through Q&A and real-time demonstrations. This creates a sense of immediacy and personal making it highly effective for real-time engagement', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1930, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01931', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which business model combines both an online store and physical retail locations?', '["Reverse auction", "Pure-click business", "Group purchasing", "Brick-and-click", "Subscription-based model"]'::jsonb, 4, 'In a Brick-and-click model combines a physical storefront (brick) with an online presence (click), allowing a company to serve customers both in-store and online', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1931, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01932', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following is not considered an e-business?', '["B2C", "B2E", "B2B", "A2C", "C2C"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "A2C".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1932, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01933', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following statements accurately distinguishes between Weak AI and Strong AI?', '["Weak AI can perform tasks without human while Strong AI cannot", "Weak AI is designed for specific while Strong AI possesses general intelligence comparable to a human", "Weak AI can understand emotions and while Strong AI operates without any understanding of context", "Weak AI requires a constant internet while Strong AI can function offline", "Weak AI is used for while Strong AI is primarily used for complex problem-solving"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Weak also known as narrow refers to AI systems that are designed to perform specific tasks or solve particular problems (like voice assistants or recommendation systems)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1933, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01934', 12, 'General ICT', 'Considering the operation of an e -commerce website as a which of the following is a functional requirement?', '["The website should have a visually appealing layout and design", "The website should allow users to filter products by and rating", "The website should load quickly and efficiently on all devices", "The website should have a customer review section for feedback", "The website should offer various payment options for users"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is option 2) The website should allow users to filter products by and rating. bv A functional requirement describes specific actions or functions a system must perform to meet user needs', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1934, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01935', 12, 'General ICT', 'If the user inputs 5, what will the output be ?', '["115", "105", "120", "200", "100"]'::jsonb, 3, 'When the user inputs 5, the function will calculate the factorial of 5, which is 5! = 5 × 4 × 3 × 2 × 1 = 120. the recursive calls start', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1935, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01936', 12, 'General ICT', 'Nowadays there are many websites that sell goods online in our country. Through you can buy goods not only with credit cards but also with cash on delivery option. Which of the following is the right type of business for these sevices?', '["B2C", "B2B", "C2B", "B2E", "B2G"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: B2C stands for Business to Consumer. This model involves businesses selling goods or services directly to individual consumers. It is the most common model in the retail industry', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1936, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01937', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following statements regarding computer technology in the future world is false?', '["Tactics will be created that work very quickly", "Techniques will be created to make the daily activities of man very easy", "A lot of smaller tricks will spawn. Wml%u fndfydauhla jkq", "More tricks will be created that harm human performance", "Techniques will emerge that use little human intervention"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: advancements in computer technology typically focus on increasing processing speeds and improving efficiency. For faster processors and algorithms are developed to perform tasks quickly', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1937, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01938', 12, 'General ICT', 'In a MAS of traffic lights (agents) controlling an lights adapt based on neighboring traffic density. one agent fails and always shows green. What is the most likely emergent effect?', '["Smooth traffic", "Local congestion at the intersection", "System-wide traffic collapse", "No effect", "Traffic lights alternate automatically"]'::jsonb, 2, 'In a MAS for traffic each agent (light) communicates with its neighbors and adapts its signals according to traffic density. This coordination helps traffic flow smoothly and prevents jams. iqugj', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1938, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01939', 12, 'General ICT', 'What is the output for this code', '["sunil kamal nimal", "sunil nimal", "kamal", "nimal", "sunil"]'::jsonb, 2, 'It iterates over each tuple in the records list. Each tuple has the format. If the marks (r[2]) are less than 50, it uses continue to skip printing. If marks are 50 or it prints the name (r[1]) with a space. th records marks)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1939, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01940', 12, 'General ICT', 'When a wave or signal is transmitted through copper the wires get heated. So what is the name given to the noise caused by', '["Induced Noise", "Cross Talk", "Thermal Noise", "Impulse Noise", "Power line Noise"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is 3) Thermal Noise. Thermal also known as Johnson-Nyquist this type of noise is generated by the random motion of electrons in a conductor (like copper wires) due to thermal agitation. As the temperature the electrons move leading to more noise', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1940, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01941', 12, 'General ICT', 'A person made a payment from his bank card to get a camera through the website. What does this deal belong to?', '["G2C", "C2B", "B2C", "B2B", "B2G"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "B2C".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1941, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01942', 12, 'General ICT', 'In which type of business model do multiple suppliers compete by lowering their prices to win a contract?', '["Group purchasing", "Reverse auction", "Pure-click business", "Brick-and-click", "Affiliate marketing"]'::jsonb, 2, 'This question is about different types of business models. The question asks which business model involves multiple suppliers competing by lowering their prices to win a contract. This is usually a "reverse where the roles are reversed compared to a traditional auction', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1942, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01943', 12, 'General ICT', 'What is the method of checking the outputs corresponding to the inputs without regard to the inner workings of a program?', '["White box testing", "Unit testing", "Accepting testing", "Integrated testing", "Black box testing"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Correct answer: "Black box testing".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1943, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01944', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which business model involves a group of buyers coming together to negotiate better pricing for goods or services?', '["Brick-and-click", "Reverse auction", "Group purchasing", "Pure-click business", "Crowdsourcing"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Group purchasing".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1944, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01945', 12, 'General ICT', 'A person has a used smartphone that they no longer need. He sells it online through where individuals can buy and sell items to each other', '["B2C", "C2B", "C2C", "B2B", "B2E"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The scenario described belongs to the category of C2C (Consumer to Consumer) transactions. In C2C individuals sell goods or services directly to other typically facilitated by online platforms such as Craigslist or OLX. C2C b-jHdmdrfha" mqoa', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1945, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01946', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which cable type is immune to electromagnetic interference (EMI) and is often used in hospitals or industrial environments?', '["UTP (Unshielded Twisted Pair", "STP (Shielded Twisted Pair", "Coaxial cable", "Fiber optic cable", "RJ45 cable"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "Fiber optic cable".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1946, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01947', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following is not a step in Pulse Code Modulation (PCM)?', '["Sampling the analog signal", "Quantizing the sampled signal", "Encoding the quantized values", "Modulating the frequency of the signal", "Converting digital signal back to analog"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "Modulating the frequency of the signal".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1947, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01948', 12, 'General ICT', 'What is the primary goal of man-machine coexistence in a work environment?', '["To completely replace human workers with machines", "To integrate human skills and machine capabilities to enhance overall productivity and", "To ensure that machines operate independently without human", "To limit human interaction with machines to prevent", "To focus solely on improving machine disregarding human"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "To integrate human skills and machine capabilities to enhance overall productivity and".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1948, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01949', 12, 'General ICT', 'Reverse auctions are most commonly used in', '["Online shopping by in dividual consumers", "Procurement and supply chain management by organizations", "Selling antiques and collectibles", "Buying and selling stocks in the stock exchange", "Peer-to-peer consumer transactions"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Incorrect. Online shopping is mostly fixed price or forward auction (buyers bid higher), not reverse auctions. Option 2: Correct. Reverse auctions are mainly used by organizations to let suppliers compete by lowering prices. Option 3: Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1949, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01950', 12, 'General ICT', 'What is a key advantage of black-box testing over white-box testing?', '["It ensures all code paths are covered. th", "It allows for efficient testing without knowledge of the internal code structure", "It provides insight into code optimization. th", "It helps identify unused code segments. th", "It ensures complete statement coverage. th"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Black-box testing focuses on checking the functionality of a program based on its inputs and outputs without considering how the internal code works. Testers do not need access to the source they test the system as an end user ensuring that all features behave as expected', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', NULL, 1950, 'A/L Past Paper Series')
